<title>CHINA: China software sales seen at $2.4 bln in 2000.</title>
<headline>China software sales seen at $2.4 bln in 2000.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's domestic sales of computer software are expected to reach 20 billion yuan ($2.4 billion) by the year 2000, the Economic Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Software sales in 1996 were worth 9.0 billion yuan, up 32 percent from 6.8 billion yuan the previous year. Imported software accounted for about 57 percent of last year's total, the official newspaper said.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
